@@ -37,6 +37,19 @@ When a Turn ends, each submitted plan appears in its final artifact area, using
 
 A review without a logged invocation also opens automatically. Its complete text lives only in the tab’s navigation memory, and the pending review card can reopen it. Reloading the page loses that text; an expired preview directs the user back to a pending review. Plans opened from an embedded child conversation use the visible sidebar while retaining the child’s address for document reads.
 
+### Commenting on a pending plan
+
+Select text in the full plan to add a comment. Saved selections stay highlighted;
+hover to read the note, or click to edit or delete it. The same composer card
+switches from Plan review to Plan revision when comments exist. Individual or
+selected comments can be deleted; deleting the last one restores Plan review.
+Revise plan sends the comments immediately, preserving any existing composer draft
+and attachments.
+Cancel plan dismisses the review and clears its comments. Completed reviews are
+read-only. Comments are stored in this browser per Session and request, without
+a server-side history. If the original text changes, an unresolved note remains
+in the card with Original text changed instead of highlighting unrelated text.
+
 ### Failures
 
 Admission failures (`matched: false`, business errors, transport faults) surface as an inline error and the chip stays until the projection confirms the exit.
@@ -55,6 +68,18 @@ Plan cards derive from native `tool/call` or PTC dispatch arguments through a Co
 
 The framework-bound `usePlans(turn)` exposes only submitted-plan data for that Turn. Chat indexes membership on Node updates and orders this collection when read; card rendering neither scans the transcript nor subscribes to other Turns or Node kinds.
 
+`ui-user-questions` owns the single `conversation.plan-review.surface` seat and
+the pending lifecycle. This plugin provides that seat and shares a Session store
+with the preview and a UI-free input overlay. The overlay clears a staged set
+of comments only when its exact revision text appears as a durable user message;
+failed sends and queued input retain the notes. Submission uses the existing
+Session prompt path without changing the composer draft. For a live review,
+feedback enters the next-step inbox before the existing non-approval answer
+releases its wait; continued reviews keep their existing dismissal behavior.
+Editing a submitted comment keeps the newer note. Preview highlights are Range geometry
+overlays, so Markdown nodes are not rewritten. An open editor holds the existing
+pending focus timer and releases it on close, unmount, or read-only transition.
+
 </details>
 
 -----
